From ec5274c7519228e0f7ded90568eab2c9b0514bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:31:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/97] threading: fix lost resume of create-suspended threads

ThreadStartRoutine published kSuspended (waking WaitStarted) before
setting suspend_count_=1 in a second critical section. A Resume() in
between saw count 0 and returned false, so the thread waited forever:
the WWE13 intermittent boot hang (Wwise AK::IOThread never started) and
load-time freezes (extra never-started guest threads). Set count and
state in one critical section, wait in the same scope, and drain the
suspend semaphore token Resume() posts for the start path.

Unit test [thread_start]: 5,000 immediate resumes + yield variant; a
test-only delay hook (REXGLUE_BUILD_TESTS) makes the old shape fail
deterministically. Gate: 3 simultaneous boots, 3x1500 s, no hang/freeze.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
